  "text": "The drawbacks next: the safe-temperature rule matters. Whole pork cuts need to reach 145 degrees Fahrenheit, then rest for at least 3 minutes. Overcooking can dry it out fast. Loin is not very forgiving once it sails past the sweet spot. Some prepackaged options have salty water added. Check the label if you want plain pork without the extra salt.",
